    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/monochrome/1-d/68-huebler42ndParallel-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "Douglas Huebler: Site Sculpture Project: 42° Parallel Piece, 1968",
      "width": "395",
      "height": "180",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "14 locations ('A' through 'N') are towns existing either exactly or approximately on the 42° Parallel in the United States. Locations have been marked by the exchange of certified postal receipts sent from and returned to 'A' – Truro, Massachusetts.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/monochrome/1-d/94-dibbetsMnmntALaMmreDArago-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "Jan Dibbets:\n\nMonument à la Mémoire d'Arago, 1994",
      "width": null,
      "height": null,
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Related issues: Continuity",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The uncountable cardinality of line and plane was thematized in\nHenry Flynt's \"word piece\" above, and in monochromes by Christer\nHennix.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A curious problem regarding the continuum was raised by Kazimir Malevich (1922): \"Since we can find no indivisible units in this world it is\nobviously extremely difficult to prove the existence of matter.\"",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "References",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Kazimir Malevich: \"A Letter to the Artists of Holland\", 1922. In: K.S. Malevich: Essays on Art, Vol. I. Copenhagen: Borgen, 1968, pp. 183-187.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "La Monte Young: Compositions. In: La Monte Young & Jackson Mac Low (eds.): An Anthology. New York, 1963.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Compiled by Remko Scha, 2005-2010",
      "links": []
    }
